# Project Report — Smart Street Lights

## Introduction

Smart Street Lights is a prototype automation system developed using Arduino and sensors to simulate intelligent energy-efficient street lighting.

## Aim

To develop a basic automated street lighting system capable of reducing unnecessary electricity usage.

## Components Used

- Arduino UNO
- LDR Sensor
- IR Sensor
- LEDs
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires

## Applications

- Smart cities
- Energy-saving systems
- Automated public lighting
- Embedded learning projects

## Conclusion

The project successfully demonstrated basic automation concepts using sensors and embedded systems.
